// causal/ — causal inference: SCMs, do-calculus and effect estimation.
//
// The question this package answers is "what would have happened if", which
// needs three things the rest of the tree does not provide: a structural causal
// model to intervene on, the do-operator to express the intervention, and a way
// to differentiate a counterfactual through all of it.
//
// linear_gaussian_scm.mbt is the substrate -- a linear Gaussian SEM with
// solvable covariances -- and do_calculus, counterfactual_reasoning and
// dragonnet all sit on it. It is used by exactly those two and nothing else,
// which is why it belongs here rather than in core/.
//
// autodiff/ is the other half. An effect estimator is an expectation over a
// reparameterised sample, so its gradient goes through the sampling as well as
// the model; autodiff_tape is what lets do_calculus differentiate an
// intervention without a hand-derived chain rule per estimator.
//
// `sim.mbt` stays in the root -- it is the simulator the SCM is fitted against,
// which is infrastructure rather than causal inference.
import {
  "riantr/snn_mbt/core",
  "riantr/snn_mbt/nn",
  "riantr/snn_mbt/activ",
  "riantr/snn_mbt/optim",
  "riantr/snn_mbt/autodiff",
}
